OL,3,GNEWSAOfficers who died on duty
OL,4,Arecognised in national honour
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe families of two police officers who
OL,7,Fdied while serving with Isle of Man
OL,8,FConstabulary are to receive the
OL,9,FElizabeth Emblem, a national honour
OL,10,Fconferred by the King.
OL,12,FSgt Jack Cretney and PC Gordon Black
OL,13,Fwill be formally recognised when the UK
OL,14,Fgovernment announces this year's
OL,15,Frecipients for the accolade on
OL,16,FThursday.
OL,18,FCretney died in separate incidents in
OL,19,F1958 and 1966 respectively.
OL,23,APub: 06-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
